INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content (path, body, version, updated_at, updated_by) VALUES ('src/content/opportunities/africa-young-innovators-for-health-award-2026-for-ai-solutions-in-family-planning.md', '---
title: Africa Young Innovators for Health Award 2026 for AI Solutions in Family
  Planning
category: Grants
organization: Ouagadougou Partnership and Speak Up Africa
deadline: 2026-11-06
location: Africa
type: Grant
image: https://www.ifpma.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/partner-yifha-logo.png
organization_logo: https://www.ifpma.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/partner-yifha-logo.png
og_image: https://www.ifpma.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/partner-yifha-logo.png
apply_url: https://airtable.com/app5SydDS6iBcZxov/pagzvUiX3wQswK5ua/form
---
**About the opportunity:**



The Africa Young Innovators for Health Award is run by the Ouagadougou Partnership and Speak Up Africa. It aims to find and support young African innovators who are using AI to tackle family planning challenges across the continent.



The organisers want practical, responsible and inclusive solutions that respond to real needs of users or health systems. This includes solutions that can work where internet connections or infrastructure are limited. Applicants fill in an online form about themselves, their team and their innovation, including how it uses AI, the impact it expects to have and how it could be put into practice. The form takes about 15 to 20 minutes, and questions marked with an asterisk must be answered.



Shortlisted applicants may be asked for extra documents. They will also be expected to take part in a hackathon, a final pitch and an award ceremony, which run from 30 November to 3 December 2026. The award suits young innovators and health-tech teams with a working prototype who want funding and visibility for their idea.



**Who can apply:**



* Africans aged 18 to 35
* Applicants who live in an African country
* Applicants who apply through a civil society or private-sector organisation
* Innovations that use AI to improve access to family planning
* Solutions that have reached prototype or MVP stage



**What you get:**



* A share of $50,000 awarded among four winners



**Official link:** Use the Apply button on this page to go straight to the official application. Always confirm the latest details and requirements on Ouagadougou Partnership and Speak Up Africa''s official page before applying.



**Reminder:** Use the "Never miss this deadline" box at the top of this page to add the deadline to your Google Calendar or Apple / Outlook calendar, so you don''t miss it.
', 1, '2026-11-09T14:52:56.798Z', 'seed');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content (path, body, version, updated_at, updated_by) VALUES ('src/content/opportunities/ai-for-human-rights-ai4hr-peer-learning-programme-for-youth-focused-organisations.md', '---
title: AI for Human Rights (AI4HR) Peer-Learning Programme for Youth-Focused
  Organisations
category: Other
organization: Global Campus of Human Rights
deadline: 2026-11-04
location: Hybrid. Online workshops and mentoring, plus a two-day in-person
  workshop in Venice, Italy.
type: Programme
apply_url: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=diOk2RYx20qEwS4UOPBIWHLpHN5FydxFlwe-pQS9pvRURExPVUxZRjBLVjlWWDZETlBGTjYyT1cwSC4u&route=shorturl
description: This programme pairs youth-focused human rights organisations with
  NGOs that already use AI in their work, so they can learn from each other.
  Participants shape their learning around their own needs, such as documenting
  rights violations or strengthening advocacy. It runs from January to early
  July 2027 and is part of a wider 2024 to 2029 research effort to build an AI
  for Human Rights Toolkit. If your organisation works with young people and is
  curious about AI, this is a low-barrier way in, since no AI experience is
  needed.
---
#### This programme pairs youth-focused human rights organisations with NGOs that already use AI in their work, so they can learn from each other. Participants shape their learning around their own needs, such as documenting rights violations or strengthening advocacy. It runs from January to early July 2027 and is part of a wider 2024 to 2029 research effort to build an AI for Human Rights Toolkit. If your organisation works with young people and is curious about AI, this is a low-barrier way in, since no AI experience is needed.

## Who can apply:

* Human rights organisations that are youth-led, or that mainly serve young people aged 15 and above
* Organisations with no prior AI experience (a clear learning goal and genuine curiosity matter most)
* Organisations from Global Majority countries, who are especially encouraged to apply
* Organisations that can commit 1 to 2 representatives to both the online and in-person parts



## What you get:

* Guidance from NGOs experienced in using AI
* Online workshops
* A two-day workshop in Venice, with participation costs covered, including travel and accommodation
* A learning path tailored to your organisation’s needs
* Any additional funding or stipend: Not stated



## How to apply:

Fill in the online application form before the deadline. Describe your organisation and its work with young people, and include links to your website or social media. Set out what you want to learn from the programme and how it connects to your work. Provide the names and CVs of 1 to 2 people who will take part.



**Official link:** Use the Apply button on this page to go straight to the official application. Always confirm the latest details and requirements on the Global Campus of Human Rights official page before applying.



**Tip**: Be specific about your learning goal. “Using AI to organise and verify evidence of violations” is more convincing than a general interest in AI.
', 1, '2026-11-09T14:52:56.798Z', 'seed');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content (path, body, version, updated_at, updated_by) VALUES ('src/content/opportunities/ai-video-creator.md', '---
title: AI Video Creator
category: Jobs
organization: BuzzyBooth.com
deadline: 2026-11-02
location: Remote
type: Full Time
image: https://workablehr.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/account/logo/352642/logo
organization_logo: https://workablehr.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/account/logo/352642/logo
og_image: https://workablehr.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/account/logo/352642/logo
apply_url: https://jobs.workable.com/view/j3iV7xCvMbRWJtSGaiSwe8/remote-ai-video-creator---video-ads-%26-social-media-reels-in-nigeria-at-buzzybooth.com
---
**About the opportunity:**

BuzzyBooth.com is recruiting a creator who can turn ideas into finished, scroll-stopping videos using AI generation tools. The company says it wants someone who can take a project all the way from concept to final edit, rather than someone who only writes prompts or produces random AI clips.



Day to day, you would make video ads and short-form content for platforms such as Facebook, Instagram, TikTok and YouTube. That includes developing concepts, hooks, scripts and storyboards, then combining AI-generated footage with real footage, voiceovers, sound effects, captions and music. You would also produce several versions of the same ad to test different hooks and messaging, and keep up with new AI video tools and social media trends.



The role suits someone who loves experimenting with new tools, understands what makes a viewer keep watching in the first few seconds, and can produce several high-quality videos each week without constant direction.



**Who can apply:**

* Mid-level creators with proven experience making AI-generated video ads or social media Reels
* Applicants with a strong portfolio of real AI video projects they have produced
* Applicants experienced with AI video tools such as Google Veo, Kling AI, Runway, Sora, Higgsfield or similar
* Applicants with solid editing skills in CapCut, Adobe Premiere Pro, After Effects or comparable software
* Creators who can make realistic AI videos that look polished and natural
* Applicants who understand hooks, storytelling, pacing and audience retention
* People who can work independently, take feedback well and deliver consistently



**Official link**: Use the Apply button on this page to go straight to the official application. Always confirm the latest details and requirements on BuzzyBooth.com’s official page before applying.



**Tip**: Build a short portfolio showing complete videos from concept to final edit, ideally with a few versions of the same ad that test different opening hooks.



**Reminder**: Use the “Never miss this deadline” box at the top of this page to add the deadline to your Google Calendar or Apple / Outlook calendar, so you don’t miss it.
', 1, '2026-11-09T14:52:56.798Z', 'seed');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content (path, body, version, updated_at, updated_by) VALUES ('src/content/opportunities/anthony-udokwu-foundation-scholarship-2027-2028-for-university-students.md', '---
title: Anthony Udokwu Foundation Scholarship 2027/2028 for University Students
category: Scholarships
organization: Anthony Udokwu Foundation
deadline: 2027-01-28
location: Nigeria
type: Scholarship
image: https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcQ0AgRhxxvQ252xJEmEgbL86Sb272kp8YAP9u8tDKUcow&s
