apply_url: https://anzisha.org/apply/
---
**About the opportunity:**



The Anzisha Fellowship identifies and supports young African entrepreneurs who are already building and growing real businesses. Each year, selected fellows join a multi-year programme designed to strengthen their ventures, speed up growth and increase their ability to create jobs.



Applications for the 2027 intake opened on 29 September 2026, and applying costs nothing. The organisers evaluate applications from November 2026 to March 2027 and announce the new fellows in May 2027. Your business must operate in Africa and serve African customers or beneficiaries, and you need to show real activity, such as customers, revenue or beneficiaries. Having only an idea is not enough.



The fellowship suits young founders who are already running a business or social venture, can give it at least 20 hours a week and want long-term support to grow it.



**Who can apply:**



* African citizens aged 15 to 22
* Founders of an existing business or social venture
* Applicants who can show real business activity, such as customers, revenue or beneficiaries
* Applicants who can commit at least 20 hours a week to the venture
* Businesses that operate in Africa and serve African customers or beneficiaries



**What you get:**



* Business development support
* Mentorship
* Access to a multi-year fellowship programme



**Official link:** Use the Apply button on this page to go straight to the official application. Always confirm the latest details and requirements on Anzisha''s official page before applying.



**Tip:** Read the official application guide before you start, and gather proof of your customers, revenue or beneficiaries so you can show real activity.



**Reminder:** Use the "Never miss this deadline" box at the top of this page to add the deadline to your Google Calendar or Apple / Outlook calendar, so you don''t miss it.
', 1, '2026-11-09T14:52:56.798Z', 'seed');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content (path, body, version, updated_at, updated_by) VALUES ('src/content/opportunities/awareness-africa-education-fund-2026-2027.md', '---
title: "Awareness Africa Education Fund 2026/2027 "
category: Scholarships
organization: Awareness Africa
deadline: 2026-10-31
location: Nigeria
type: Scholarship
image: https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRe25tEUTI0kSIcO7KOvuczba-1eXsSXgV7XdRUROx0FQ&s=10
og_image: https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRe25tEUTI0kSIcO7KOvuczba-1eXsSXgV7XdRUROx0FQ&s=10]
apply_url: https://www.awarenessafrica.org/
---
**About the opportunity:**



The Awareness Africa Education Fund is a need-based scholarship for a Nigerian student who is about to begin undergraduate studies at a federal or state university in the 2026/2027 academic session. It is meant for someone whose financial situation could stop them from starting university, or make it very hard to do so.



The fund contributes towards school fees and compulsory registration fees. Applicants were directed to an online application page, and the closing date was 31 October 2026. Applications for this round are now closed.



It suits students who have shown commitment to their studies, have a genuine financial need and are starting at a federal or state university. If you were planning to apply, check Awareness Africa''s official channels for any later round.



**Who can apply:**



* Nigerian students starting undergraduate studies at a federal or state university in the 2026/2027 session
* Students who have shown academic commitment
* Students with a genuine financial need that could prevent or seriously hinder them from starting university



**What you get:**



* Financial support towards school fees
* Support towards compulsory registration fees





**Official link**: This call has closed. Always confirm the latest details, and whether a new round has opened, on Awareness Africa''s official page.



**Tip**: Follow Awareness Africa''s official pages so you can see the next call early and prepare your documents before it opens.
', 1, '2026-11-09T14:52:56.798Z', 'seed');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content (path, body, version, updated_at, updated_by) VALUES ('src/content/opportunities/carewave-aspire-scholarship-programme-casp.md', '---
title: "Carewave Aspire Scholarship Programme (CASP) "
category: Scholarships
organization: Care Wave Foundation
deadline: 2026-11-08
location: Nigeria
type: Scholarship
image: https://api.carewavefoundation.org/attachments/file-1790075854490-12651212.JPG
og_image: https://api.carewavefoundation.org/attachments/file-1790075854490-12651212.JPG
apply_url: https://carewavefoundation.org/scholarships/SCH-2026-946543
---
**About the opportunity:**



Care Wave Foundation is a registered non-profit organisation based in Abuja. Its work covers education, healthcare access, elder care, economic stability and support for underserved communities. The Carewave Aspire Scholarship Programme (CASP) is its merit- and need-based undergraduate scholarship, designed especially for students from vulnerable or financially disadvantaged communities.



The initial award covers one academic year and is worth ₦500,000. It is meant to help with education and living costs, and the foundation''s guidance says this may include tuition fees, books, transport and upkeep. Renewal is not automatic. Continued support depends on academic performance, meeting the programme''s requirements and staying in good academic standing, and recipients may need to send progress reports every term.



Applications are made online through the foundation''s scholarship portal and include a motivation letter of 600 to 1,000 words. Applications are reviewed and verified, and shortlisted candidates may be invited to an interview, either online or in person. The scholarship suits students with strong academic potential, real financial need, integrity and leadership potential, and a clear commitment to finishing their degree.



**Who can apply:**



* Nigerian citizens
* Students who have secured admission into an eligible Federal University in Nigeria
* Applicants for undergraduate study
* Students with strong academic performance
* Students who can show genuine financial need
* Students from vulnerable or financially disadvantaged communities
* Applicants who show integrity, leadership potential and commitment to their education
* Applicants who can write a motivation letter of 600 to 1,000 words



**What you get:**



* An annual award of ₦500,000
* Initial support that covers one academic year
* Support for educational and living-related costs
* Possible coverage of tuition fees, books, transport and upkeep, depending on the approved support
* Consideration for renewal in later academic sessions, based on performance and compliance
* No IELTS requirement



**Official link**: Use the Apply button on this page to go straight to the official application. Always confirm the latest details and requirements on Care Wave Foundation''s official page before applying.



**Tip**: Write your motivation letter early and check that it is between 600 and 1,000 words, since a letter outside that range can cost you your application.



**Reminder**: Use the "Never miss this deadline" box at the top of this page to add the deadline to your Google Calendar or Apple / Outlook calendar, so you don''t miss it.
', 1, '2026-11-09T14:52:56.798Z', 'seed');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content (path, body, version, updated_at, updated_by) VALUES ('src/content/opportunities/codesria-research-grants-on-gender-academic-freedom-and-associational-life-in-african-universities.md', '---
title: "CODESRIA Research Grants "
category: Grants
organization: Council for the Development of Social Science Research in Africa (CODESRIA)
deadline: 2027-01-16
location: Open to researchers based at African universities and research
  institutions. Delivery format (in person or virtual) is not stated.
type: Grant
image: /uploads/codesria_appel_bourses_en_fr-1.png
og_image: ""
apply_url: https://apply.codesria.org/grants-subventions/
description: >
  CODESRIA is funding research that looks at how universities in Africa are
  changing, with a focus on gender, academic freedom and the strength of student
  and staff associations on campus. Successful researchers get 15 months of
  support to carry out original studies, join peer-learning workshops and
  produce work that can shape policy. It suits scholars who want their research
  to be published and used in real policy conversations.
---
## **Who can apply:**

Researchers affiliated with a recognised higher education or research institution in Africa African scholars in the diaspora, as long as they partner with colleagues at an African-based institution. Individuals or teams of 3 to 5 people (interdisciplinary, multi-institution or multi-country teams are strongly encouraged)Women scholars, early-career academics and staff at less well-resourced universities are specifically encouraged to apply. Applicants with unfinished deliverables from earlier CODESRIA-funded projects are discouraged from applying

## What you get:

15 months of research support. Access to knowledge-exchange workshops and peer-learning forums. Opportunities to contribute to public dialogue and policy engagement. Award amount: Applicants submit a draft budget of USD 5,000 to USD 15,000)

## How to apply:

* Choose your focus: gender and associational life, or academic and intellectual freedom (studies linking the two are especially welcome).
* Prepare a recent CV (for teams, one for every member).
* Write a proposal synopsis of up to 4,000 words covering your research question, a review of recent literature, your conceptual framework, methodology and timeline, a draft budget and your planned outputs, both scholarly and non-scholarly. 
* Include a draft budget between USD 5,000 and USD 15,000.
* Get a formal letter of affiliation or endorsement from your institution. 
* Submit everything online through the CODESRIA application portal before the deadline (click the apply link below).



**Tip**: Prioritised sub-themes include digital transitions and AI in universities, university governance and funding models, and graduate outcomes, so tie your idea to one of them. Questions can go to tgf@codesria.org.
', 1, '2026-11-09T14:52:56.798Z', 'seed');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content (path, body, version, updated_at, updated_by) VALUES ('src/content/opportunities/dalai-lama-fellows-2027-fellowship.md', '---
title: "Dalai Lama Fellows 2027 Fellowship "
category: Fellowships
organization: Dalai Lama Fellows
deadline: 2026-11-11
location: Global
type: Fellowship
image: https://dalailamafellows.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dlf-home-hero-full.webp
organization_logo: https://dalailamafellows.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dlf-home-hero-full.webp
og_image: https://dalailamafellows.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dlf-home-hero-full.webp
apply_url: https://dalailamafellows.com/apply/
---
**About the opportunity:**



Dalai Lama Fellows is a global programme for young people leading projects that create social change. The 2027 group will include 15 to 20 fellows. The formal fellowship year runs from April 2027 to March 2028, after which fellows join the LifeLong Fellows global leadership and learning community.



During the year, fellows keep working on their own social change project while taking part in an online learning platform, one-to-one coaching calls and group learning calls. They also learn and practise contemplative approaches and attend an online Contemplative Leadership Assembly in May 2027. The organisers estimate that full participation takes about 12 hours a month, not counting the time you spend on your project.



The fellowship suits people who already run a social change project, or who have a concrete plan and the skills, resources and community connections to launch one during the year. The organisers prefer applicants with an ongoing project and at least a year of experience working with the community they serve.



**Key dates:**



Applications close on 11 November 2026 at 22:00 UTC, which is 11:00 PM in Nigeria. Finalists are invited to interviews in January 2027, and fellows are selected and told in February 2027. Online onboarding takes place in March 2027.



**Who can apply:**



* Applicants aged 20 to 36 as of 1 April 2027
* Applicants fluent in written and spoken English
* Applicants with a current social change project, or a clear plan to launch one and the means to do it
* Applicants with in-depth knowledge of the community and issue their project addresses, preferably with at least one year of experience working with that community
* Applicants who want to learn and take part in contemplative practices throughout the year
* Applicants who can commit to all parts of the programme, including the online learning platform and coaching and group calls
* Applicants who can attend the virtual Contemplative Leadership Assembly in May 2027



**What you get:**



* An online learning platform
* One-to-one coaching calls
* Group learning calls
* Membership of the LifeLong Fellows global leadership and learning community



**How to apply:**



1. Check that you meet the age, English and project requirements above.

2. Fill in the applicant background and overview section.

3. Answer the short essay questions.

4. Record and submit your video.

5. Upload your resume or CV.

6. Arrange your letter of recommendation.

7. Submit your application and all materials before 22:00 UTC on 11 November 2026.



**Official link:** Use the Apply button on this page to go straight to the official application. Always confirm the latest details and requirements on Dalai Lama Fellows'' official page before applying.



**Tip**: Start your essays and video early, and ask your recommender now, since a late letter can leave your application incomplete.



**Reminder:** Use the "Never miss this deadline" box at the top of this page to add the deadline to your Google Calendar or Apple / Outlook calendar, so you don''t miss it.
', 1, '2026-11-09T14:52:56.798Z', 'seed');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content (path, body, version, updated_at, updated_by) VALUES ('src/content/opportunities/developer-experience-engineer-at-ritual.md', '---
title: Developer Experience Engineer at Ritual
category: Jobs
organization: Ritual
deadline: 2026-11-30
location: Remote or hybrid
type: Job
image: https://s7-recruiting.cdn.greenhouse.io/external_greenhouse_job_boards/logos/400/225/000/original/Mark_%E2%80%BA_Transparent_Black.png?1699449714
organization_logo: https://s7-recruiting.cdn.greenhouse.io/external_greenhouse_job_boards/logos/400/225/000/original/Mark_%E2%80%BA_Transparent_Black.png?1699449714
og_image: https://s7-recruiting.cdn.greenhouse.io/external_greenhouse_job_boards/logos/400/225/000/original/Mark_%E2%80%BA_Transparent_Black.png?1699449714
apply_url: https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/ritual/jobs/4614247007
---
**About the opportunity:**



Ritual is building a blockchain designed from the start to support AI-native applications, and its private testnet is already live. Its first product, Infernet, lets developers use AI models both on-chain through smart contracts and off-chain.



As a Developer Experience Engineer, you would design and build the tools that make it easy for developers to build on Ritual. That includes development frameworks for AI-enabled chains similar in spirit to Foundry, fast local environments for testing, command-line tools and SDKs, and debugging and simulation tools for AI and blockchain interactions. You would also find the points where developers struggle and fix them, write clear documentation and tutorials, run workshops and hackathons, and help grow an open-source community around the tools.



The role suits an engineer who has built developer tools that people enjoy using, understands smart contracts and the EVM, and can explain technical ideas well in writing and in person. It also suits someone who takes full ownership of their work and is comfortable in a fast-moving environment.



**Who can apply:**



* Engineers with strong experience in at least one of Rust, TypeScript or Python
* Applicants who have contributed to open-source projects and libraries
* Applicants with a record of building developer tools that developers love to use
* Applicants with a deep understanding of EVM architecture and smart contract development
