description: Kinship’s Nature Culture Fellowship supports people who use
  storytelling, art and culture to drive social and environmental change. It
  runs from February to August 2027, includes a micro-grant of USD 1,000 to USD
  2,000, and is open to applicants worldwide.
---
**About the opportunity:**

The Nature Culture Fellowship is run by Kinship for people who believe that stories, art and culture can change how societies relate to nature and to one another. It aims to build a global movement of change-makers who work through culture.

The fellowship runs in two stages between February and August 2027. First is a Learning Journey, starting on 5 February 2027, where fellows explore storytelling, art as activism, systems thinking and ways of building respectful relationships with the living world. Then comes a Project Implementation phase, where each fellow turns what they have learned into a project, supported by a micro-grant and mentorship. It is open to applicants from any country, and the application can be completed in English, Spanish, Portuguese or French. It suits community-rooted creatives, organisers and storytellers who want time, guidance and a little funding to make their ideas real.

**Who can apply:**

* Individuals with real roots and influence in their communities. 
* People who can commit 3 to 7 months to the programme
* Self-motivated applicants who are open to new perspectives and to unlearning old ones
* Connectors who want to break down systemic barriers and who value creativity, collaboration and storytelling
* Applicants who are focused on lasting projects and partnerships
* Applicants from any country (the application is available in English, Spanish, Portuguese and French)

**What you get:**

* A micro-grant of USD 1,000 to USD 2,000 for your project
* Mentorship from professionals
* A Learning Journey starting on 5 February 2027
* Opportunities to grow your work locally, regionally and globally



**How to apply:**

* Go to the official application page.
* Choose your language: English, Spanish, Portuguese or French.
* Fill in the application form before the deadline.
* Wait for the selection results, expected in mid-January 2027.
* Official link: Use the Apply button on this page to go straight to the official application. Always confirm the latest details and requirements on Kinship’s official page before applying.

**Reminder:** Tap the Reminder button on this page to add the deadline to your calendar so you don’t miss it.

**Tip**: Focus your application on the community you already work in and the story you want to tell. The fellowship is looking for people with existing local influence.
', 1, '2026-11-09T14:52:56.798Z', 'seed');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content (path, body, version, updated_at, updated_by) VALUES ('src/content/opportunities/nnpc-snepco-national-university-scholarship-2026.md', '---
title: "NNPC-SNEPCo National University Scholarship 2026 "
category: Scholarships
organization: NNPC-SNEPCo
deadline: 2026-11-30
location: Nigeria
type: Scholarship
image: https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRKJ0hDBTly_Zb81kekt_OvCuHstgMF1wxOwHFdXwBacA&s=10
og_image: https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRKJ0hDBTly_Zb81kekt_OvCuHstgMF1wxOwHFdXwBacA&s=10
apply_url: https://candidate.scholastica.ng/schemes/NNPCLTDSNEPCo26
---
**About the opportunity:**



The NNPC-SNEPCo National University Scholarship is run by SNEPCo for itself, NNPC Limited and its co-venture partners. It aims to promote academic excellence and build the skills of young Nigerians. Successful applicants receive a yearly grant that continues until they finish their undergraduate programme, as long as they keep up their grades.



Applications are made online through the scholarship portal only. Candidates who meet the eligibility criteria are invited to a monitored computer-based test. The top 10 candidates from each of the 36 states and the FCT are then shortlisted for academic verification before any award is offered. Anyone found to have falsified their results is disqualified.



It suits strong second-year students at public universities who have a high CGPA and do not already hold another oil and gas industry scholarship.



**Who can apply:**



* Nigerian citizens
* Students currently in their second year of full-time study at a public Nigerian university accredited by the NUC
* Students with a minimum CGPA of 3.5 on a 5-point scale, or the equivalent on other grading systems
* Students who are not beneficiaries of any other scholarship from an oil and gas industry entity, national or international
* Female candidates are strongly encouraged to apply



**What you get:**



* A yearly grant from your second year until you complete your undergraduate degree
* You must keep a minimum CGPA of 3.5 each session to continue receiving the award



**How to apply:**



1. Register an account on the scholarship portal and activate it using the link sent to your email.

2. Log in and fill in your personal and educational details, plus your National Identification Number (NIN) if you have one.

3. Upload scanned copies of your documents: a passport photograph (JPEG, white background, not more than 200 KB), your admission letter, UTME result, O''Level and any A''Level, OND or NCE results, a letter of identification from your state of origin, your 100 level CGPA results, and the completed government declaration form.

4. Make sure the name on your application matches the name on all your documents, and check every upload for errors.

5. Select the scholarship under Active Scholarships and click Apply Now to submit.

6. Download your profile from the portal, get your Head of Department to sign it, and upload the signed copy.

7. If you did not have a NIN earlier, register with the National Identity Management Commission (NIMC) to get one, then update your application with it.



**Official link:** Use the Apply button on this page to go straight to the official application. Always confirm the latest details and requirements on SNEPCo''s official page before applying.



**Tip:** Start collecting your documents now, especially the letter of identification from your state of origin, the signed profile and your NIN, because these depend on other offices and can take time.



**Reminder:** Use the "Never miss this deadline" box at the top of this page to add the deadline to your Google Calendar or Apple / Outlook calendar, so you don''t miss it.
', 1, '2026-11-09T14:52:56.798Z', 'seed');
